GIMP Palette
Name: Corsair (pipeline test)
Columns: 5
#
# THIS IS NOT THE CANONICAL PALETTE. assets/palette.gpl is.
#
# Scoped to the corsair pipeline test in this directory and nothing else.
#
# Every colour here was MEASURED, not chosen: it is the output of
#
#   mgf-tools extract-palette --input <reference> --output palette.gpl
#
# with the generated hue-family names (amber-1, magenta-0, ...) replaced by
# role names, which is the one edit that tool asks you to make. The RGB values
# are the reference's own, byte for byte, with a single exception noted below.
#
# That matters more than it sounds. The first version of this palette was
# invented by reading hex codes off a screenshot, and it was wrong in a way no
# gate could ever report: check-palette only asks whether the art matches the
# palette, so art and palette invented together agree perfectly and are both
# wrong. Measuring the source is the only thing that breaks that loop.
#
# The exception: the reference outlines in #000000, and every palette in this
# repo shares `outline` #1A1A1A (check-palettes enforces it). extract-palette
# rewrites the darkest low-chroma entry to the spine and conform-sprite then
# moves the art onto it -- 84 px, a 0.2178 Oklab move, the largest single
# change in the import and the only deliberate one.
#
# 0 ramp collisions, verified by Palette.FindRampCollisions via check-palettes.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 80   0   0	crimson-0-shadow
176  40  96	crimson-1
248  64 112	crimson-2-hilite
248 116 108	blush
248 210 194	skin
137  90  27	leather-0-shadow
216 160  56	leather-1
248 216 112	gold
  0  37  91	denim-0-shadow
 35  73 120	denim-1
 54 111 164	denim-2-hilite
 80  80  80	steel
214 212 213	bone-1
255 255 255	bone-2-hilite
